## 2 · Grey Section Rules (`bg-[#FAFAFA]`)

- Background: always exactly `#FAFAFA`
- Headings: `text-heading`
- Body text: `text-muted`
- No motif
- **Cards are BLACK** — dark cards on a light grey background create intentional contrast

### Grey section bg snippet
```astro
<Fragment slot="bg">
  <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[#FAFAFA] dark:bg-slate-900/30"></div>
</Fragment>
```

### Card on Grey bg
```astro
<div class="rounded-lg border border-accent/60 bg-[#222] p-4 md:p-5 flex flex-col shadow-none outline-none">
  <h3 class="text-[16px] md:text-[18px] font-medium font-heading leading-[130%] mb-2 text-white">{title}</h3>
  <p class="text-[13px] md:text-[14px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-white/60">{description}</p>
</div>
```

Optional left accent bar for compact cards: add `border-l-4 border-l-accent` to the card div.

### Ghost button on Grey bg

```astro
<a href="/path" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-6 py-3 rounded-md border-2 border-black text-black font-semibold text-[15px] leading-snug hover:bg-black hover:text-white transition-colors duration-200">
  Button Label
</a>
```

- Border: `border-2 border-black`
- Text: `text-black`
- Hover: `hover:bg-black hover:text-white`

### Step/numbered circle on Grey bg

When a step or process uses a numbered circle indicator, the circle must be dark with yellow text:

```astro
<div class="shrink-0 w-9 h-9 rounded-full bg-[#222] flex items-center justify-center font-heading font-medium text-[15px] text-accent mt-0.5">
  {step}
</div>
```

- Circle bg: `bg-[#222]`
- Number text: `text-accent` (yellow)
- Never use `bg-primary`, `bg-white`, or any other colour for step circles on a grey background

