## 3 · Black Section Rules (`bg-black` + motif)

- Background: `bg-black`
- Motif: `simple.svg` accent yellow at **8% opacity**, top-to-bottom fade
- Headings: `text-white`
- Body text: `text-white/70`
- Disclaimer / secondary text: `text-white/50`
- **Cards are dull black with yellow border**

### Black section bg snippet
```astro
<Fragment slot="bg">
  <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-black"></div>
  <div class="absolute inset-0" style="-webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, black 0%, transparent 100%); mask-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, black 0%, transparent 100%);">
    <div
      class="absolute inset-0 opacity-[8%]"
      style={`background-color: var(--aw-color-accent); -webkit-mask-image: url('${simplePattern.src}'); mask-image: url('${simplePattern.src}'); -webkit-mask-size: cover; mask-size: cover; -webkit-mask-mode: luminance; mask-mode: luminance;`}
      aria-hidden="true"
    ></div>
  </div>
</Fragment>
```

### Card on Black bg
```astro
<div class="rounded-lg border border-accent/60 bg-[#222] p-6 flex flex-col">
  <h3 class="text-[22px] md:text-[26px] font-medium font-heading leading-[130%] mb-3 text-white">{title}</h3>
  <p class="text-[14px] md:text-[15px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-white/60">{description}</p>
</div>
```

Use `isDark={true}` on `WidgetWrapper` for black sections. Pass `cardClass="border border-accent/60 bg-[#222]"` to `Features2` or `Testimonials` components.

### Ghost button on Black bg

```astro
<a href="/path" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-6 py-3 rounded-md border-2 border-accent text-white font-semibold text-[15px] leading-snug hover:bg-accent hover:text-black transition-colors duration-200">
  Button Label
</a>
```

- Border: `border-2 border-accent` (yellow)
- Text: `text-white`
- Hover: `hover:bg-accent hover:text-black`

